"""
Dew-point temperature from a saturation pressure and relative humidity input.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.Others.MoistAir.DewTemperature`. The original Modelica model
read a moist-air `port` and used `Modelica.Media`'s saturation pressure / relative humidity
calls. Dyad has no equivalent fluid medium, so this version is signal-based: callers supply
the saturation pressure `P_sat` (Pa) and relative humidity `RH` (0..1) directly, and the
component returns the dew-point temperature in Kelvin using Magnus' formula:

```math
T_\mathrm{dew} = 273.15 + \frac{241.88 \, \ln(P_\mathrm{vap} / 610.78)}{17.558 - \ln(P_\mathrm{vap} / 610.78)}
```

with `P_vap = P_sat · RH`.

This is the same formula as in the upstream model, only the data plumbing is different.
"""
component DewTemperature
  "Saturation pressure of moist air at port"
  P_sat = RealInput()
  "Relative humidity in 0..1"
  RH = RealInput()
  "Computed dew-point temperature [K]"
  Tdew = RealOutput()

  variable P_vap::Pressure
relations
  P_vap = P_sat * RH
  Tdew = 273.15 + (241.88 * log(P_vap / 610.78)) / (17.558 - log(P_vap / 610.78))
end
